-- 🚨 NEGATIVE fixture for the TYPE-CONSTRUCTOR HOMONYM guard (#2327 finding 2).
--
-- `tyCanon` compares type constructors by BARE NAME — it has no resolver — so
-- this file's own `Set` canonicalises identically to stdlib's `set.Set`, and
-- `insertSet` relaxes onto the stdlib name `insert`.  Before the guard, the rule
-- fired here and told the author to "use the stdlib version" of a function whose
-- type does not even mention the same `Set`: not merely noisy but TYPE-INCORRECT
-- advice, the same bare-name-across-modules hazard the stdlib index is keyed to
-- avoid for stdlib VALUE names.
--
-- A file that declares its own `Set` is talking about its own `Set`, so the rule
-- must stay silent.  Do not "fix" this fixture by renaming the local type.
export
data Set a = Empty | Node a (Set a) (Set a)

export
insertSet : Ord a => a -> Set a -> Set a
insertSet _ s = s
